Lolly patch 0002: colours from the active design system.

Why: upstream's palette (src/ui/palette.ts) is the single colour source,
written to --c-* at boot and imported as constants by the CodeMirror theme
and the canvas readers. This routes all of them through ONE resolved table
the utility derives from the app around it (light or dark as the app is, in
the design system's colours, contrast-checked, packages/rondo/editor/theme.ts),
with upstream's hex as the fallback. Inside Lolly each constant is a
var(--c-*) reference, so when the app's theme changes while the editor is
open the boot script rewrites the custom properties and everything repaints,
CodeMirror's theme included. It also
gathers the few literals that must follow the table: three syntax hues, the
ink on the run button and on an accent fill, the event flash, the record dot
and the scrim behind code while visuals are on.

Applied by scripts/vendor-rondocode.ts with git apply --directory=packages/rondo/upstream.

